From: AymanRGab <aymanrgab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] clk: qcom: clk-rcg2: Keep force-enable in
 shared_enable to fix downstream branch

clk_rcg2_shared_enable force-enables the RCG (CMD_ROOT_EN=1), writes
the stored configuration, runs update_config, then clears force-enable
(CMD_ROOT_EN=0). When the Common Clock Framework calls shared_enable on
the RCG (parent) and then clk_branch2_enable on the branch (child), the
RCG is already turned off by the time the branch tries to start. The
branch halt check polls for CBCR_CLK_OFF to clear, but with no clock
from the parent, the bit never clears and the call returns -EBUSY.

This affects RCGs that are single-consumer (used by only one downstream
branch) and do not have HW_CLK_CTRL_MODE set, such as the MCLK RCGs in
camcc-sm8250. After a GDSC power cycle the RCG registers are in reset;
shared_enable is the only path that turns them on, and the subsequent
force-off defeats that purpose.

Remove the clk_rcg2_clear_force_enable call so the RCG stays running
after shared_enable. clk_rcg2_shared_disable still force-offs the RCG
when the last consumer releases it.

Fixes: 3b766ffd1951 ("clk: qcom: clk-rcg2: Add support for
clk_rcg2_shared_ops")
Signed-off-by: AymanRGab <aymanrgab@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/clk-rcg2.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-rcg2.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-rcg2.c
index 55a66d5620d5..40f3fcc9cbeb 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-rcg2.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-rcg2.c
@@ -1440,7 +1440,7 @@ static int clk_rcg2_shared_enable(struct clk_hw *hw)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	return clk_rcg2_clear_force_enable(hw);
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static void clk_rcg2_shared_disable(struct clk_hw *hw)
-- 
